    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d1c7badd-1fca-5018-a733-b0b166ddd5f5",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=16 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=-8 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=-3.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(-3)=-8.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}=-8-(-3)=-5.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=-5$ and ${x}_{3}=-3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(-5)-(-3)=16.\n$$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}=16-(5)-(3)=8.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=8$, ${x}_{2}=-5$, and ${x}_{3}=-3.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n⟨8,-5,-3⟩.\n$$",
